  "known_ambiguities": [
    "PROPERTY CASE: graph properties are camelCase (filePath, lineRange, signatureHash, fileHash, nameTokens) except snake_case ones (created_at, updated_at, last_seen_commit, deleted_at, summary_embedding, last_commit_sha). The property is 'filePath', NOT 'file_path'. MCP tool results, however, use snake_case 'file_path' / 'line_range'. A consumer writing raw Cypher must use filePath; a consumer using MCP must use file_path.",
    "Repo node carries 'name' (not 'slug'); other nodes carry 'repo'. The Repo node has no 'repo' property.",
    "Function vs Method: class methods are emitted as Function nodes with 'function:' ids; Method/make_method_id exist but are unused. Two same-named, same-signature methods in different classes of one file would collide on id.",
    "Enum nodes: normalisation maps 'enum' to the 'class:' id prefix while the label is Enum; no source emits enums today, and no Enum uniqueness constraint exists.",
    "Section ids share the 'doc:' prefix with Document ids; extract_id_parts() only partially parses function/method ids.",
    "Layer id is built with the raw layer name (not slugified via make_layer_id).",
    "MENTIONS is declared and produced by the markdown source but deferred ('<symbol>:' targets) and never persisted; consumers mapping MENTIONS will see none. DOCUMENTS only exists after 'link-docs'; TESTS only after 'test-map'.",
    "INSTANTIATES/CONTAINS/DEFINES/EXTENDS/REFERENCES/EXPOSES_ENDPOINT/CALLS_HTTP are declared in domain/schema.py but never written.",
    "RENAMED_FROM is written old-file -> new-file, which reads backwards from its name.",
    "'repo' is the user-supplied slug verbatim (case preserved). CLI 'ingest' defaults it to the directory name (or parent name for generic dirs src/lib/app/source/main/code); the MCP ingest_repo uses 'repo_slug' as given (may be 'owner/name' or a bare name). The CLI resolves case-insensitively against existing Repo nodes, but the MCP/pipeline path does not, so 'DevOnHire' and 'devonhire' can coexist as distinct repos. Consumers MUST normalise (last path segment, lower-case, strip .git) before comparing.",
    "Default string properties are written as '' (not null) for language/signature/signatureHash/fileHash/filePath; 'layer' is null (property absent) when undetected.",
    "Embedding dimension: vector indexes are created with EMBEDDING model dimensions (default 384, bge-small); unknown model names silently fall back to 384, and an existing index with another dimension is not recreated (IF NOT EXISTS).",
    "list_projects previously matched on Repo.slug (nonexistent) -> fixed in this branch to Repo.name; a Repo node count of 0 for older CodeKG builds is a symptom.",
    "get_node/impact queries match '(n {id: $id})' without a label; ids are only guaranteed unique per label-constraint, not globally, and an unlabelled id lookup is a full scan.",
    "Node 'type' in MCP results is the first label that is not CodeNode/DocNode (e.g. 'Function'), but trace_call_chain's chain[].type is labels(n)[0] (label order is not guaranteed)."
  ]
}
